WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:02.089 --> 00:00:05.701
♪ ♪

2
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:13.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

3
00:00:22.239 --> 00:00:24.807
<i>Previously on</i> Star Trek:
Strange New Worlds...

4
00:00:24.981 --> 00:00:28.376
<i>BATEL [over comms]: To any Federation
vessels in range. need help.</i>

5
00:00:28.506 --> 00:00:29.725
<i>Under attack by the Gorn.</i>

6
00:00:29.855 --> 00:00:31.118
<i>APRIL: The Federation's at</i>

7
00:00:31.248 --> 00:00:32.297
<i>a dangerous point
in our relationship</i>

8
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:33.598
<i>with the Gorn Hegemony.</i>

9
00:00:33.772 --> 00:00:36.123
UHURA: It looks like
a demarcation line.

10
00:00:36.253 --> 00:00:37.911
UNA: With Parnassus Beta
and all their forces

11
00:00:37.994 --> 00:00:39.114
on the far side of the line.

12
00:00:39.213 --> 00:00:40.649
<i>PIKE: Unfortunately.
that is where</i>

13
00:00:40.779 --> 00:00:42.089
I believe our people
are being held.

14
00:00:42.172 --> 00:00:44.087
<i>I don't plan on
leaving them behind.</i>

15
00:00:44.218 --> 00:00:47.525
[growling]

16
00:00:47.656 --> 00:00:50.050
If somewhere in my
head is the answer

17
00:00:50.224 --> 00:00:51.881
<i>to saving the</i> Enterprise. <i>then
that's a risk I have to take.</i>

18
00:00:51.964 --> 00:00:55.098
Take this. It'll help you hide.

19
00:00:55.664 --> 00:00:57.753
[echoing]: Run!

20
00:00:57.883 --> 00:00:59.972
Montgomery Scott
at your service.

21
00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.322
ORTEGAS: How are you not dead?

22
00:01:01.452 --> 00:01:03.628
Well. I figured out how
to hide in plain sight.

23
00:01:03.759 --> 00:01:05.413
You built a Gorn transponder?

24
00:01:05.543 --> 00:01:06.936
Eh. basically. to a scanner.

25
00:01:07.023 --> 00:01:08.546
the shuttle looked
like a Gorn ship.

26
00:01:08.633 --> 00:01:11.245
Could you build another
device like the one you made?

27
00:01:11.375 --> 00:01:13.247
-What's happening?
-Captain Batel is in need

28
00:01:13.377 --> 00:01:15.336
-of immediate sedation.
-Happened yesterday.

29
00:01:15.466 --> 00:01:17.033
I'm not giving up on her.

30
00:01:17.207 --> 00:01:18.527
I have no intention
of doing that.

31
00:01:18.643 --> 00:01:20.127
Captain. the transporter's
not currently picking up

32
00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:21.298
anyone on the surface.

33
00:01:23.518 --> 00:01:24.823
[shouting]

34
00:01:27.565 --> 00:01:29.828
Admiral April's ordering
our immediate withdrawal.

35
00:01:29.959 --> 00:01:31.787
<i>SPOCK: The colonists
and the landing party</i>

36
00:01:31.874 --> 00:01:33.049
<i>appear to have been beamed up</i>

37
00:01:33.223 --> 00:01:35.269
-by the Gorn.
-Orders. Captain?

38
00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:41.144
<i>ANNOUNCER: And now.
the conclusion.</i>

39
00:02:02.339 --> 00:02:03.688
UNA: Orders. Captain?

40
00:02:03.819 --> 00:02:05.473
MITCHELL: Shields at 50%.

41
00:02:05.603 --> 00:02:07.997
-UNA: Captain.
-MITCHELL: Captain.

42
00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.175
[alarm blaring]

43
00:02:12.262 --> 00:02:13.437
UNA: Orders. Captain?

44
00:02:13.611 --> 00:02:15.570
Uhura. repeat
April's last order.

45
00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:16.780
UHURA: Retreat and rendez...

46
00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:19.661
Retreat and rendezvous
with the fleet. sir.

47
00:02:19.835 --> 00:02:22.098
-He gave coordinates.
-But he didn't say immediately?

48
00:02:24.579 --> 00:02:26.498
-All right. who's got ideas?
-Diversionary tactics.

49
00:02:26.581 --> 00:02:27.669
We're too boxed in.

50
00:02:27.843 --> 00:02:29.410
Vent the nacelles.
create a cloud?

51
00:02:29.540 --> 00:02:31.340
-We need to be able to see.
-Jam their comms

52
00:02:31.455 --> 00:02:32.935
so they can't
coordinate attacks.

53
00:02:33.065 --> 00:02:34.328
That's it. That's the one.

54
00:02:37.853 --> 00:02:40.334
The Gorn use light for
ship-to-ship messaging.

55
00:02:40.508 --> 00:02:42.035
UHURA: I'm modulating
the deflector array

56
00:02:42.118 --> 00:02:44.207
to emit a spectrum. Should
confuse them for a bit.

57
00:02:48.472 --> 00:02:50.043
All right. now how do we beam
our people back to <i>Enterprise?</i>

58
00:02:50.126 --> 00:02:51.958
Scans indicate the Gorn ships
are transport-resistant.

59
00:02:52.041 --> 00:02:53.477
So. even if we get
past the shields.

60
00:02:53.608 --> 00:02:55.701
-we need authorization codes.
-No time to hack codes.

61
00:02:55.784 --> 00:02:57.612
Retreat and rescue.

62
00:02:57.742 --> 00:02:59.052
It's the best of a
bunch of bad options.

63
00:02:59.135 --> 00:03:00.401
So how do we track
this specific ship

64
00:03:00.484 --> 00:03:01.833
across light-years of space?

65
00:03:01.964 --> 00:03:03.226
SPOCK: Wolkite. A rare element

66
00:03:03.357 --> 00:03:05.141
that contains
subspace gauge bosons.

67
00:03:05.315 --> 00:03:06.664
If we modified a
homing beacon...

68
00:03:06.751 --> 00:03:08.884
The Gorn would see a beacon
coming from a mile away.

69
00:03:09.014 --> 00:03:10.277
Not if it's a torpedo.

70
00:03:11.974 --> 00:03:13.541
We tag 'em with a dud.

71
00:03:13.715 --> 00:03:15.155
The Gorn won't know
what we're up to.

72
00:03:19.982 --> 00:03:21.418
MITCHELL: Shields at 30%.

73
00:03:21.505 --> 00:03:22.728
For this to succeed. we
still need to penetrate

74
00:03:22.811 --> 00:03:23.971
the Gorn's defensive systems.

75
00:03:24.073 --> 00:03:25.353
MITCHELL: We've
been hitting them

76
00:03:25.509 --> 00:03:27.124
with everything we've
got. it doesn't do much.

77
00:03:27.207 --> 00:03:29.513
Uh. energy shields
work on harmonics.

78
00:03:29.644 --> 00:03:31.123
If we find the
right frequency...

79
00:03:31.254 --> 00:03:32.516
We can ram the ship.

80
00:03:32.647 --> 00:03:33.778
SPOCK: Indeed.

81
00:03:33.952 --> 00:03:35.592
When our shields make
contact with theirs.

82
00:03:35.693 --> 00:03:37.351
they will create a destructive
interference pattern

83
00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:39.349
and momentarily interrupt
both frequencies.

84
00:03:40.394 --> 00:03:42.487
MITCHELL: With our shields
down. we'd be sitting ducks.

85
00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:45.011
-We'd only have one shot.
-That's all we need. Mitchell. bring us around.

86
00:03:45.094 --> 00:03:47.662
head-to-head with the destroyer.

87
00:03:47.792 --> 00:03:49.403
Time to play a game of chicken.

88
00:04:01.937 --> 00:04:04.200
UHURA: All decks.
prepare for impact.

89
00:04:04.331 --> 00:04:05.379
Full impulse on your
orders. Captain.

90
00:04:05.462 --> 00:04:06.811
Inertial dampeners to maximum.

91
00:04:06.985 --> 00:04:09.249
Everybody hold onto something.

92
00:04:09.901 --> 00:04:13.122
Una... let's hit it.

93
00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.443
PIKE: Fire torpedoes.

94
00:04:34.796 --> 00:04:36.841
-Helm. warp us out of here.
-On it.

95
00:04:36.928 --> 00:04:38.495
Hang in there. guys.

96
00:04:47.374 --> 00:04:49.071
<i>PIKE: Space.</i>

97
00:04:50.551 --> 00:04:52.292
<i>The final frontier.</i>

98
00:04:54.424 --> 00:04:57.819
<i>These are the voyages of
the starship</i> Enterprise.

99
00:04:58.994 --> 00:05:01.997
<i>Its five-year mission:</i>

100
00:05:02.127 --> 00:05:05.000
<i>to explore strange new worlds...</i>

101
00:05:07.089 --> 00:05:09.613
<i>...to seek out new life</i>

102
00:05:09.787 --> 00:05:12.224
<i>and new civilizations...</i>

103
00:05:13.487 --> 00:05:17.404
<i>...to boldly go where
no one has gone before.</i>

104
00:05:17.534 --> 00:05:20.145
♪ ♪

105
00:05:47.608 --> 00:05:49.566
♪

106
00:06:13.895 --> 00:06:15.810
♪ ♪

107
00:06:35.917 --> 00:06:38.746
Captain. we've arrived
at the rendezvous point.

108
00:06:38.833 --> 00:06:41.313
The USS <i>Pablo Picasso</i>
is hailing to greet us.

109
00:06:41.488 --> 00:06:42.967
It's Admiral April. sir.

110
00:06:43.141 --> 00:06:45.274
He's beaming aboard
now to debrief.

111
00:06:45.405 --> 00:06:48.843
-[sighs] More needles?
-Yes. just a few more pokes.

112
00:06:48.973 --> 00:06:51.846
I mean. without these.
your body will go necrotic

113
00:06:51.976 --> 00:06:53.500
in the stasis field. so...

114
00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:56.764
-Things turn purple. It's not pretty.
-Mm.

115
00:06:56.894 --> 00:06:58.635
I've never been
frozen solid before.

116
00:06:58.722 --> 00:07:00.463
It's not an exciting prospect.

117
00:07:00.594 --> 00:07:03.771
Well. as soon as we work out
this little Gorn infection.

118
00:07:03.945 --> 00:07:05.816
you'll be up and around again.

119
00:07:05.947 --> 00:07:08.863
So this could be like a Rip
Van Winkle thing for me.

120
00:07:08.950 --> 00:07:11.431
I see you more as
a Sleeping Beauty.

121
00:07:13.389 --> 00:07:15.913
Listen. I meant
what I said before.

122
00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:18.046
The moment it looks
like me or the crew.

123
00:07:18.176 --> 00:07:19.221
you take me out.

124
00:07:19.351 --> 00:07:22.442
Don't think about that.

125
00:07:22.616 --> 00:07:24.444
Stasis will prevent
you and the Gorn

126
00:07:24.531 --> 00:07:26.968
from any type of
cellular growth.

127
00:07:27.142 --> 00:07:29.274
There's another
side to the coin.

128
00:07:31.102 --> 00:07:33.583
Whatever it takes.

129
00:07:35.498 --> 00:07:37.413
Whatever it takes. I promise.

130
00:07:37.587 --> 00:07:41.199
-I'm. uh. I'm gonna give you a sedative now.
-[device clicks]

131
00:07:41.373 --> 00:07:44.333
And when you wake up.
you will be Gorn-free.

132
00:07:55.866 --> 00:07:59.000
-[grunting]
-[alarms sounding]

133
00:08:01.393 --> 00:08:04.092
Epinephrine and
neutralizer. stat!

134
00:08:05.572 --> 00:08:07.443
Her body's rejecting the serum.

135
00:08:12.579 --> 00:08:14.102
Sickbay to bridge.

136
00:08:14.232 --> 00:08:16.060
<i>Uh. I have an update.
and it's not good.</i>

137
00:08:16.191 --> 00:08:18.236
Bottom line it for me.

138
00:08:18.367 --> 00:08:21.065
Captain Batel is
allergic to cryoserum.

139
00:08:21.196 --> 00:08:23.807
<i>We can't put her in stasis.</i>

140
00:08:23.938 --> 00:08:25.548
So she's back on
a ticking clock?

141
00:08:25.679 --> 00:08:29.204
The Gorn will hatch
from her body in. um...

142
00:08:29.334 --> 00:08:31.728
[sniffles] in less than a day.

143
00:08:33.513 --> 00:08:35.384
I'm stuck trying to
find a treatment.

144
00:08:35.515 --> 00:08:38.300
Um... uh...

145
00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:40.607
maybe if Joseph was
here. I could...

146
00:08:42.217 --> 00:08:46.221
I'm sending help. Christine...

147
00:08:48.266 --> 00:08:51.139
...I believe in you. Help her.

148
00:08:51.269 --> 00:08:53.707
I'll do my best. Captain.

149
00:08:55.056 --> 00:08:57.580
SPOCK: Captain. I
may not be a doctor.

150
00:08:57.711 --> 00:08:59.673
but I will dedicate all of
my abilities to Captain Batel

151
00:08:59.756 --> 00:09:01.279
until her Gorn infection

152
00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:03.586
is... resolved.

153
00:09:12.508 --> 00:09:13.944
<i>PIKE: Just stand by?</i>

154
00:09:14.075 --> 00:09:16.381
You have the entire fleet
out there ready to go.

155
00:09:16.512 --> 00:09:18.470
APRIL: It's a show of force.

156
00:09:18.645 --> 00:09:20.472
First we need to
establish patrols.

157
00:09:20.603 --> 00:09:24.302
Do they really think the
Gorn are just gonna stop

158
00:09:24.433 --> 00:09:26.870
and go home after they raided
those colonies? [scoffs]

159
00:09:27.001 --> 00:09:29.177
Look. it's a tough situation.
but we have to manage it

160
00:09:29.307 --> 00:09:30.961
one piece at a time.

161
00:09:31.092 --> 00:09:33.228
-There are innocent lives at stake. Bob.
-And I get that.

162
00:09:33.311 --> 00:09:35.836
But it's happening outside
of our jurisdiction.

163
00:09:35.923 --> 00:09:37.098
Oh. come on. Bob.

164
00:09:37.272 --> 00:09:38.752
Apart from your
reckless dogfight.

165
00:09:38.926 --> 00:09:41.319
these attacks do not
involve the Federation.

166
00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:42.973
We have regulations. Chris.

167
00:09:43.147 --> 00:09:44.326
So. because it's non-Federation
citizens that are dying.

168
00:09:44.409 --> 00:09:45.802
we do nothing?

169
00:09:45.889 --> 00:09:47.068
We have an obligation
to our member worlds.

170
00:09:47.151 --> 00:09:49.023
Billions of lives.

171
00:09:49.153 --> 00:09:50.811
To rush into a fight right
now puts all of them at risk.

172
00:09:50.894 --> 00:09:52.330
We can't do it.

173
00:09:52.461 --> 00:09:54.119
We're still recovering
from the Klingon War.

174
00:09:54.202 --> 00:09:56.813
You are absolutely right. and
the Gorn sense our weakness.

175
00:09:56.944 --> 00:09:58.728
We are prey.

176
00:10:03.254 --> 00:10:04.908
They will push
this Hegemony line

177
00:10:05.082 --> 00:10:07.345
further and further
into Federation space.

178
00:10:07.519 --> 00:10:08.608
And you know they will.

179
00:10:08.738 --> 00:10:10.135
And by the time we
actually get around

180
00:10:10.218 --> 00:10:12.655
to doing something about it...

181
00:10:12.786 --> 00:10:14.135
it'll be way too late.

182
00:10:17.704 --> 00:10:19.140
I heard about the landing party.

183
00:10:19.270 --> 00:10:21.403
Yeah. and a couple
hundred colonists. too.

184
00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:24.536
And Marie?

185
00:10:26.843 --> 00:10:28.802
She's in sickbay.

186
00:10:37.462 --> 00:10:39.773
Officially. your orders are to
monitor the demarcation line

187
00:10:39.856 --> 00:10:41.597
for any encroachment
by the Gorn.

188
00:10:46.341 --> 00:10:49.213
Okay. And unofficially?

189
00:10:53.435 --> 00:10:55.916
How do we punch back and
show them we aren't prey?

190
00:10:58.266 --> 00:10:59.615
Yeah. I can do that.

191
00:10:59.746 --> 00:11:01.443
<i>PELIA: This
contraption of yours.</i>

192
00:11:01.617 --> 00:11:02.923
what's it supposed to do again?

193
00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:06.100
Emit a polarized EM signature
that tricks the Gorn

194
00:11:06.187 --> 00:11:07.322
into thinking we're one of them.

195
00:11:07.405 --> 00:11:08.711
It's like a cloaking device.

196
00:11:08.798 --> 00:11:10.495
And how. exactly.
does it do that?

197
00:11:10.626 --> 00:11:12.458
Ah. if I'm being honest.
I don't really remember.

198
00:11:12.541 --> 00:11:13.934
I was kind of in the moment.

199
00:11:14.021 --> 00:11:16.110
Well. now I'm going to
ask a silly question.

200
00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:17.981
to which I'm pretty
sure I know the answer.

201
00:11:18.155 --> 00:11:19.983
[sighs] Not this again.

202
00:11:20.114 --> 00:11:21.554
It's like being back
in lecture hall.

203
00:11:21.637 --> 00:11:23.121
How would you know that?
You were never there.

204
00:11:23.204 --> 00:11:25.728
I was there. in the back.

205
00:11:25.859 --> 00:11:27.125
Did you record a
work-in-progress log

206
00:11:27.208 --> 00:11:28.949
while you were
jury-rigging this up?

207
00:11:29.079 --> 00:11:31.560
What. you mean as the Gorn
were tearing our ship apart?

208
00:11:31.691 --> 00:11:34.737
First rule in engineering.
Scotty: write it down.

209
00:11:34.824 --> 00:11:36.434
There's a reason
we track our work

210
00:11:36.565 --> 00:11:38.915
no matter what the
circumstance. and this.

211
00:11:39.089 --> 00:11:41.918
this right now. this is
precisely the reason.

212
00:11:42.049 --> 00:11:43.833
Pardon the interruption.

213
00:11:44.007 --> 00:11:45.447
How long before you
get that working?

214
00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:46.923
Oh. Captain Pike. the thing is.

215
00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:48.882
it worked on my wee shuttle.

216
00:11:49.012 --> 00:11:50.583
-but the <i>Enterprise</i> is...
-How soon do you need it. Captain?

217
00:11:50.666 --> 00:11:53.190
We're headed into Gorn
space. so now would be good.

218
00:11:53.277 --> 00:11:56.846
It'll be up and working before
we cross the Hegemony line.

219
00:11:56.977 --> 00:11:59.588
I'm counting on it. as are the
lives of everyone on board.

220
00:11:59.675 --> 00:12:00.680
We're going after
our missing crew.

221
00:12:00.763 --> 00:12:01.883
with or without that device.

222
00:12:03.157 --> 00:12:05.463
Understand?

223
00:12:05.637 --> 00:12:07.770
Well. that's no pressure.

224
00:12:07.857 --> 00:12:09.729
♪ ♪

225
00:12:35.232 --> 00:12:38.105
<i>-YOUNG LA'AN: Mom?
-LA'AN'S MOTHER: La'An. be brave.</i>

226
00:12:39.193 --> 00:12:41.329
<i>LA'AN: Not believing you're gonna
die is what gets you killed.</i>

227
00:12:41.412 --> 00:12:43.153
<i>It's the Gorn.</i>

228
00:12:43.284 --> 00:12:44.502
<i>Wake up.</i>

229
00:12:44.633 --> 00:12:46.940
<i>-Wake up!</i>
-[screams]

230
00:12:48.071 --> 00:12:50.813
[grunting]

231
00:12:59.039 --> 00:13:00.518
[grunts]

232
00:13:05.610 --> 00:13:06.829
[yells]

233
00:13:09.092 --> 00:13:11.051
[panting]

234
00:13:31.027 --> 00:13:32.420
You can do this.

235
00:13:34.726 --> 00:13:36.467
Always start with the doctor.

236
00:13:52.875 --> 00:13:55.835
[M'Benga grunting]

237
00:14:01.449 --> 00:14:04.147
[retches]

238
00:14:05.279 --> 00:14:06.846
-[coughs]
-Okay.

239
00:14:14.941 --> 00:14:16.551
[groaning]

240
00:14:18.727 --> 00:14:22.035
Holy crap. my hand!

241
00:14:22.165 --> 00:14:23.518
-Half my hand is frickin' gone.
-LA'AN: Look at me.

242
00:14:23.601 --> 00:14:26.387
Erica. look at me.
Look at me. Relax.

243
00:14:28.128 --> 00:14:31.392
It's going to be okay.
It's going to be okay.

244
00:14:31.566 --> 00:14:34.264
[Ortegas groaning]

245
00:14:34.438 --> 00:14:36.357
M'BENGA: We can fix this
when we get back to the ship.

246
00:14:36.440 --> 00:14:38.965
ORTEGAS: Please. Okay.

247
00:14:39.095 --> 00:14:41.271
-M'BENGA: Try to stay calm.
-ORTEGAS: Okay.

248
00:14:45.928 --> 00:14:48.452
ORTEGAS: How?

249
00:14:48.583 --> 00:14:51.064
How do we get back to the ship?

250
00:14:53.414 --> 00:14:54.894
What about them?

251
00:14:56.634 --> 00:14:58.810
If we free them one at a time.

252
00:14:58.941 --> 00:15:01.726
we'll only get a handful out.

253
00:15:01.857 --> 00:15:04.251
SAM: If that. Look
how long it took

254
00:15:04.381 --> 00:15:05.905
for the four of us to get loose.

255
00:15:09.212 --> 00:15:11.345
This is a massive
digestive chamber.

256
00:15:12.476 --> 00:15:13.836
And it's working
its way through...

257
00:15:13.956 --> 00:15:16.698
looks like a-a processing
plant for fuel.

258
00:15:16.785 --> 00:15:18.700
Or just food for the Gorn.

259
00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:20.920
I don't like the idea
of being anyone's lunch.

260
00:15:22.443 --> 00:15:24.445
And even if we can wake them up.

261
00:15:24.619 --> 00:15:27.839
one or a hundred.

262
00:15:27.970 --> 00:15:31.234
we still don't have
a way out of...

263
00:15:31.408 --> 00:15:33.062
wherever this is.

264
00:15:33.236 --> 00:15:35.108
M'BENGA: One step at a time.

265
00:15:35.238 --> 00:15:37.240
Sitting here doing nothing
is a death sentence.

266
00:15:37.371 --> 00:15:38.724
SAM: And for all we know.
the Gorn were alerted

267
00:15:38.807 --> 00:15:40.678
the moment that we woke up.

268
00:15:40.852 --> 00:15:42.902
ORTEGAS: So the killer lizards
could already be on their way.

269
00:15:42.985 --> 00:15:44.338
-They're coming.
-Don't be afraid.

270
00:15:44.421 --> 00:15:45.466
La'An.

271
00:15:45.596 --> 00:15:46.858
<i>No matter what.</i>

272
00:15:47.729 --> 00:15:50.384
La'An.

273
00:15:50.471 --> 00:15:52.473
What's on your mind. Lieutenant?

274
00:15:55.171 --> 00:15:57.521
You're right.

275
00:15:57.695 --> 00:15:59.654
It's not just about us.

276
00:15:59.741 --> 00:16:02.265
All of these people
will be dead soon.

277
00:16:02.439 --> 00:16:04.050
SAM: Hey. This looks like

278
00:16:04.180 --> 00:16:05.747
an evacuation pile.

279
00:16:05.877 --> 00:16:10.839
Maybe whatever the ship
can't process. it expels.

280
00:16:11.622 --> 00:16:13.407
[chuckles]

281
00:16:14.408 --> 00:16:16.105
[squishing]

282
00:16:16.236 --> 00:16:18.020
[grunting]

283
00:16:19.674 --> 00:16:21.328
-[exhales]
-ORTEGAS: Ah.

284
00:16:24.896 --> 00:16:26.986
Weapons from a crap pile.

285
00:16:30.293 --> 00:16:33.296
Strangely. it's a step
in the right direction.

286
00:16:35.124 --> 00:16:37.300
I don't want to save a
handful of colonists.

287
00:16:37.431 --> 00:16:38.998
I want to save them all.

288
00:16:39.172 --> 00:16:41.522
Everyone that's still
alive gets home.

289
00:16:43.741 --> 00:16:46.048
Even if we have to
shoot our way out.

290
00:16:57.842 --> 00:17:00.019
♪ ♪

291
00:17:09.637 --> 00:17:10.942
[power sputters]

292
00:17:11.073 --> 00:17:13.554
Ack. bawheid.

293
00:17:13.641 --> 00:17:15.001
-That's not it.
-PELIA: The Gorn!

294
00:17:15.164 --> 00:17:16.426
The Gorn! They're here!

295
00:17:16.513 --> 00:17:17.862
Oh. shite.

296
00:17:18.037 --> 00:17:19.168
PELIA: We're doomed. Scotty.

297
00:17:19.342 --> 00:17:21.083
-No. no. no. no...
-We're all gonna die!

298
00:17:22.737 --> 00:17:24.521
SCOTTY: It's working.

299
00:17:24.695 --> 00:17:26.935
It's working. Tell the bridge
to patch it to the shields.

300
00:17:27.916 --> 00:17:29.526
What? Is it too late?

301
00:17:29.657 --> 00:17:31.532
<i>PIKE: Bridge to science lab.
What's the status down there?</i>

302
00:17:31.615 --> 00:17:34.053
<i>-We're about to enter Gorn space.</i>
-Oh. you minx.

303
00:17:34.183 --> 00:17:35.750
PELIA: It's up and
running. Captain.

304
00:17:35.880 --> 00:17:38.492
We can patch it into
the shields now.

305
00:17:38.622 --> 00:17:40.494
<i>-Excellent. Pike out.</i>
-That wasn't funny.

306
00:17:40.624 --> 00:17:42.326
-It was fun.
-You nearly gave me a heart attack.

307
00:17:42.409 --> 00:17:44.498
I did it 'cause I know you.

308
00:17:44.672 --> 00:17:47.461
-No. you don't.
-Yes. with too much time on your hands. you fall apart.

309
00:17:47.544 --> 00:17:50.417
but put a phaser to
your head and voilà.

310
00:17:50.547 --> 00:17:52.767
Why do you care what I do?

311
00:17:53.811 --> 00:17:54.986
You put up walls. Scotty.

312
00:17:55.161 --> 00:17:56.901
You're too afraid
to take a risk.

313
00:17:57.032 --> 00:17:58.816
I fixed what you wanted me to.

314
00:17:58.947 --> 00:18:00.775
And you're
insubordinate to boot.

315
00:18:00.862 --> 00:18:02.262
Well. technically
you're not my C.O.

316
00:18:02.429 --> 00:18:04.518
She went down on the <i>Stardiver.</i>

317
00:18:06.041 --> 00:18:07.390
May I be excused. sir?

318
00:18:07.477 --> 00:18:09.697
[softly]: Oh. Scotty.

319
00:18:11.786 --> 00:18:13.962
[door whooshes open]

320
00:18:17.792 --> 00:18:20.273
MITCHELL: Approaching the Hegemony
demarcation line now. sir.

321
00:18:20.403 --> 00:18:22.013
PIKE: Drop us out of warp.

322
00:18:22.144 --> 00:18:23.584
-Start Mr. Scott's transponder.
-UNA: Transponder?

323
00:18:23.667 --> 00:18:27.018
Pelia says it's more like a
modified EM pulse emitter.

324
00:18:27.106 --> 00:18:28.368
Okay. then that makes sense.

325
00:18:28.455 --> 00:18:31.501
The Gorn must not
use optical data.

326
00:18:31.632 --> 00:18:34.722
They've evolved. so they
must rely on biometrics.

327
00:18:34.852 --> 00:18:37.507
heat and EM signatures.

328
00:18:37.638 --> 00:18:39.857
Well. time to see if
it actually works.

329
00:18:39.988 --> 00:18:42.469
It should. I mean.

330
00:18:42.599 --> 00:18:45.167
unless maybe one of them
decides to look out a window.

331
00:18:45.298 --> 00:18:46.603
[device beeping]

332
00:18:46.734 --> 00:18:48.692
MITCHELL: Captain. Gorn
hunters approaching.

333
00:18:52.479 --> 00:18:54.437
Keep us steady and on course.

334
00:18:59.921 --> 00:19:02.228
So far. I don't see any windows.

335
00:19:15.719 --> 00:19:17.460
MITCHELL: It worked.

336
00:19:18.766 --> 00:19:20.424
Uhura. do we still have a
signal from the wolkite beacon?

337
00:19:20.507 --> 00:19:21.943
Aye. sir.

338
00:19:22.073 --> 00:19:24.293
It's faint and getting
weaker but still there.

339
00:19:24.467 --> 00:19:26.165
Any intel on where
they're headed?

340
00:19:26.295 --> 00:19:28.079
UNA: An uncharted
binary star system.

341
00:19:28.210 --> 00:19:30.125
The stellar activity there

342
00:19:30.256 --> 00:19:33.259
is like nothing we've
ever seen before.

343
00:19:33.389 --> 00:19:36.483
-Helm. plot a course.
-Captain. the radiation in that system is off the charts.

344
00:19:36.566 --> 00:19:38.529
At a certain point. we can
only use impulse engines.

345
00:19:38.612 --> 00:19:40.657
and our shields won't
be able to protect us.

346
00:19:40.788 --> 00:19:42.620
Understood. We'll make it quick.
Mitchell. warp factor seven.

347
00:19:42.703 --> 00:19:44.400
Aye aye. sir.

348
00:19:52.800 --> 00:19:54.410
SPOCK: Intriguing.

349
00:19:54.541 --> 00:19:56.804
The incubation has severely
altered her biochemistry.

350
00:19:56.978 --> 00:19:58.762
CHAPEL: Her body
is now as dependent

351
00:19:58.893 --> 00:20:02.026
on the Gorn hatchlings
as they are on her.

352
00:20:02.201 --> 00:20:04.768
SPOCK: The perfect
host. inseparable.

353
00:20:04.899 --> 00:20:06.466
Have you tried
microscopic debulking?

354
00:20:06.596 --> 00:20:08.903
<i>COMPUTER: Results completed.</i>

355
00:20:09.033 --> 00:20:10.474
CHAPEL: It's the last
simulation I ran.

356
00:20:10.557 --> 00:20:13.864
<i>COMPUTER: Probability
of fatality is 100%.</i>

357
00:20:14.038 --> 00:20:16.998
That's the chorus of the day.
It's every simulation I've run.

358
00:20:18.434 --> 00:20:20.784
Computer. run scenarios
for microscopic debulking

359
00:20:20.958 --> 00:20:23.309
factoring for an infusion
of Zadora extract.

360
00:20:23.439 --> 00:20:26.268
<i>-COMPUTER: Processing.</i>
-CHAPEL: An Orion street drug?

361
00:20:28.444 --> 00:20:30.838
Actually. that's
kind of brilliant.

362
00:20:31.926 --> 00:20:34.106
You are the one who taught me
to look outside of the box.

363
00:20:34.189 --> 00:20:37.323
[chuckles] It's "think."
but close enough.

364
00:20:38.149 --> 00:20:40.195
Christine.

365
00:20:42.284 --> 00:20:44.591
-I know you want to talk.
-I will be brief.

366
00:20:44.721 --> 00:20:46.070
I simply want to apologize

367
00:20:46.201 --> 00:20:47.641
for the way things
ended before you left.

368
00:20:47.724 --> 00:20:50.292
I reacted poorly.

369
00:20:50.379 --> 00:20:52.729
Apology accepted.

370
00:20:52.860 --> 00:20:54.078
We're good.

371
00:20:54.165 --> 00:20:56.820
The thought of losing you.

372
00:20:56.951 --> 00:20:58.953
it affected me deeply.

373
00:20:59.083 --> 00:21:00.781
I understand.

374
00:21:02.391 --> 00:21:04.175
This has gotten complicated.

375
00:21:04.306 --> 00:21:06.221
and I am not good
at complicated.

376
00:21:06.352 --> 00:21:10.834
And I am still going
away for three months

377
00:21:11.008 --> 00:21:13.010
to study with Roger Korby.

378
00:21:13.097 --> 00:21:16.623
When I get back. let's
just see where we are then.

379
00:21:16.753 --> 00:21:18.320
So you are saying that perhaps

380
00:21:18.494 --> 00:21:20.017
some time apart
might be good for us?

381
00:21:20.148 --> 00:21:22.411
[softly]: Spock.

382
00:21:23.891 --> 00:21:26.285
Yeah.

383
00:21:26.415 --> 00:21:28.852
But not like...

384
00:21:28.983 --> 00:21:32.552
not like "us" us.

385
00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:35.598
Like...

386
00:21:35.685 --> 00:21:37.774
us as people.

387
00:21:38.819 --> 00:21:41.038
Please don't do something
you think is romantic.

388
00:21:41.212 --> 00:21:44.085
like wait for me or something.

389
00:21:44.215 --> 00:21:46.740
<i>COMPUTER: Zadora extract
scenario completed.</i>

390
00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:50.700
<i>Probability of fatality is 100%.</i>

391
00:21:52.180 --> 00:21:54.704
SPOCK: No matter how
we approach this.

392
00:21:54.878 --> 00:21:56.619
Batel's human DNA is...

393
00:21:56.706 --> 00:21:58.317
Inadequate.

394
00:21:59.622 --> 00:22:02.059
Her body goes into shock.
blood pressure drops.

395
00:22:02.233 --> 00:22:03.409
And she dies.

396
00:22:06.063 --> 00:22:09.458
Huh. Human physiology.

397
00:22:09.545 --> 00:22:10.855
What if we gave her
some help there?

398
00:22:10.938 --> 00:22:12.200
You have an idea.

399
00:22:12.331 --> 00:22:13.810
-Illyrian.
-Illyrian DNA.

400
00:22:13.941 --> 00:22:15.290
Una's blood.

401
00:22:15.421 --> 00:22:16.948
it's designed to combat
infections in real time.

402
00:22:17.031 --> 00:22:18.772
A plasma injection
could provide a boost

403
00:22:18.902 --> 00:22:20.473
-to Batel's immunity.
-And we could attempt

404
00:22:20.556 --> 00:22:22.083
the surgery without
her going into shock.

405
00:22:22.166 --> 00:22:23.907
SPOCK: It is
against regulation.

406
00:22:24.038 --> 00:22:25.909
but it could save her life.

407
00:22:26.040 --> 00:22:28.390
Computer. run
scenario for surgery

408
00:22:28.521 --> 00:22:29.957
factoring for a
plasma transfusion

409
00:22:30.131 --> 00:22:31.045
from an Illyrian blood donor.

410
00:22:31.175 --> 00:22:33.874
<i>COMPUTER: Processing.</i>

411
00:22:34.004 --> 00:22:35.310
How did you put it once?

412
00:22:35.397 --> 00:22:37.834
Some rules are
intended to be broken?

413
00:22:37.965 --> 00:22:39.314
[laughs softly]

414
00:22:39.445 --> 00:22:41.969
Almost exactly it.

415
00:22:42.099 --> 00:22:43.579
LA'AN: There's the hangar.

416
00:22:43.710 --> 00:22:45.407
Okay.

417
00:22:45.494 --> 00:22:47.148
Everyone's clear on the plan?

418
00:22:47.278 --> 00:22:48.371
SAM: Access the
ship's mainframe.

419
00:22:48.454 --> 00:22:50.064
upload the Gorn
transporter codes...

420
00:22:50.194 --> 00:22:52.066
Get them to the <i>Enterprise.</i>

421
00:22:52.196 --> 00:22:54.764
To do that. we have to steal
a ship and fly it out of here.

422
00:22:54.938 --> 00:22:57.593
M'BENGA: That one
doesn't look guarded.

423
00:22:57.724 --> 00:22:59.465
Totally got this. not
impossible at all.

424
00:23:00.857 --> 00:23:02.772
And it's true you can
fly anything. right?

425
00:23:02.946 --> 00:23:05.079
Don't be rude. Of course I can.

426
00:23:05.209 --> 00:23:07.124
LA'AN: Okay.

427
00:23:07.211 --> 00:23:08.430
Let's get to that ship.

428
00:23:10.389 --> 00:23:11.520
This is a good plan.

429
00:23:11.694 --> 00:23:14.393
It's gonna work.

430
00:23:17.004 --> 00:23:19.136
It's good. It's-it's...

431
00:23:19.267 --> 00:23:20.921
It's a good plan. right?

432
00:23:21.008 --> 00:23:22.357
It's a good plan.

433
00:23:22.488 --> 00:23:25.186
Yeah. Yeah. Now all
we have to do is

434
00:23:25.316 --> 00:23:27.275
not get caught by the Gorn.

435
00:23:27.362 --> 00:23:30.278
[distant growling]

436
00:23:30.409 --> 00:23:32.062
-Sam.
-Why would you say that?

437
00:23:32.236 --> 00:23:34.021
What? Oh. come on.
you can't blame me.

438
00:23:34.151 --> 00:23:34.978
LA'AN: Phasers to kill.

439
00:23:35.152 --> 00:23:36.937
Time to go.

440
00:23:42.986 --> 00:23:44.423
Uhura and I have
been poring over

441
00:23:44.597 --> 00:23:46.512
all available data on the Gorn.

442
00:23:46.642 --> 00:23:48.601
Confirmed attacks.
unverified sightings.

443
00:23:48.775 --> 00:23:51.386
If it might be a Gorn.
we've checked it out.

444
00:23:51.473 --> 00:23:53.649
And there's a lot more
out there than we thought.

445
00:23:55.042 --> 00:23:56.391
UNA: You have to
squint a little.

446
00:23:56.522 --> 00:23:57.958
But every Gorn
sighting correlates

447
00:23:58.088 --> 00:24:00.264
to a pattern of
specific stellar events.

448
00:24:00.395 --> 00:24:02.702
Coronal mass ejections. I
know this already. CMEs.

449
00:24:02.832 --> 00:24:04.530
Stellar flares can
set off a frenzy.

450
00:24:04.660 --> 00:24:06.619
Yes. the attacks
follow a pattern.

451
00:24:06.749 --> 00:24:09.099
but so does Gorn inactivity.

452
00:24:09.273 --> 00:24:11.275
Uhura is the one who found it.

453
00:24:11.406 --> 00:24:12.668
There are long periods of time

454
00:24:12.799 --> 00:24:14.670
where no Gorn
activity is reported.

455
00:24:14.844 --> 00:24:16.324
Not so much as a rumor.

456
00:24:16.455 --> 00:24:18.108
UNA: And in those instances.

457
00:24:18.239 --> 00:24:20.894
there's unique stellar activity
that seems to trigger...

458
00:24:21.024 --> 00:24:22.765
-Hibernation.
-UHURA: Yes.

459
00:24:22.896 --> 00:24:25.202
We believe that the Gorn have
a long hibernation cycle.

460
00:24:25.333 --> 00:24:27.034
Under the right conditions.
they become docile.

461
00:24:27.117 --> 00:24:28.554
We can use that.

462
00:24:28.728 --> 00:24:30.168
The science team
chipped in on the math

463
00:24:30.251 --> 00:24:32.427
and was able to isolate the
presence of X-class flares

464
00:24:32.514 --> 00:24:34.821
and supra-arcade down flows
that precede their absence.

465
00:24:37.258 --> 00:24:38.912
Good work. both of you.

466
00:24:39.086 --> 00:24:40.827
UNA: There's something else.

467
00:24:41.871 --> 00:24:44.439
The data also suggests
that we could be

468
00:24:44.570 --> 00:24:47.355
at the beginning of a long
cycle of Gorn aggression.

469
00:24:47.486 --> 00:24:50.663
These attacks could
signal what could soon be

470
00:24:50.793 --> 00:24:52.578
a full-scale Gorn invasion.

471
00:24:52.708 --> 00:24:54.667
[comms chime]

472
00:24:54.797 --> 00:24:57.365
<i>MITCHELL: Dropping out of
warp in two minutes. sir.</i>

473
00:24:57.452 --> 00:24:59.062
Thank you. Mitchell. On our way.

474
00:25:06.853 --> 00:25:08.507
[door whooshes open]

475
00:25:10.204 --> 00:25:13.207
UNA: Spock and Chapel
know what they're doing.

476
00:25:13.337 --> 00:25:14.469
I trust them

477
00:25:14.600 --> 00:25:15.880
with a couple
liters of my blood.

478
00:25:17.080 --> 00:25:19.126
Thank you for that.

479
00:25:19.256 --> 00:25:21.171
They say it may
be her only hope.

480
00:25:21.302 --> 00:25:23.739
For Marie. they can
take all they want.

481
00:25:23.870 --> 00:25:25.179
This mission's already
off-the-record.

482
00:25:25.262 --> 00:25:26.786
so nothing to report.

483
00:25:28.178 --> 00:25:29.658
Chris.

484
00:25:29.789 --> 00:25:31.834
take some of your own advice.

485
00:25:32.008 --> 00:25:34.097
Focus on hope.

486
00:25:39.059 --> 00:25:42.192
<i>COMPUTER: Illyrian blood
donor scenario completed.</i>

487
00:25:42.323 --> 00:25:45.195
<i>Probability of fatality: 86%.</i>

488
00:25:45.369 --> 00:25:47.375
That's the first one that's
given her any chance at all.

489
00:25:47.458 --> 00:25:49.286
Albeit not a very high one.

490
00:25:49.373 --> 00:25:51.767
I mean. we can't do the
surgery with these odds.

491
00:25:52.812 --> 00:25:54.857
We're on to something.
Let's keep at it.

492
00:25:55.031 --> 00:25:56.816
Indeed.

493
00:26:00.123 --> 00:26:01.734
UNA: We're near
the radiation zone.

494
00:26:01.864 --> 00:26:04.127
From here on. it's
impulse engines only.

495
00:26:04.998 --> 00:26:06.434
[sighs]

496
00:26:09.393 --> 00:26:10.917
Mitchell. you've
been running nonstop.

497
00:26:11.091 --> 00:26:12.745
Call for relief.

498
00:26:12.875 --> 00:26:14.573
With respect. I'm not
leaving the station

499
00:26:14.703 --> 00:26:16.357
until we get everyone back.

500
00:26:17.532 --> 00:26:18.751
Copy.

501
00:26:20.317 --> 00:26:21.580
Thank you.

502
00:26:26.672 --> 00:26:28.195
I have the wolkite signature.

503
00:26:28.325 --> 00:26:30.240
We're coming up on
the enemy destroyer.

504
00:26:30.371 --> 00:26:32.551
-How soon can we overtake them?
-Chris. we may be too late.

505
00:26:32.634 --> 00:26:33.900
They've already entered
the radiation zone.

506
00:26:33.983 --> 00:26:35.942
If we go any deeper
into this star system.

507
00:26:36.072 --> 00:26:37.164
we put the entire crew at risk.

508
00:26:37.247 --> 00:26:38.422
Helm. full stop.

509
00:26:41.034 --> 00:26:43.993
Put the long-range visual
up on the main screen.

510
00:26:47.431 --> 00:26:49.259
Is it me. or does it look like

511
00:26:49.433 --> 00:26:51.827
that ship is going to
fly right into that star?

512
00:26:53.568 --> 00:26:55.614
I see it. I don't believe it.

513
00:26:55.744 --> 00:26:57.398
Telemetry confirms. Captain.

514
00:26:57.528 --> 00:26:59.487
-We have to do something.
-Look.

515
00:27:02.229 --> 00:27:03.709
MITCHELL: Did they
just lose power?

516
00:27:05.058 --> 00:27:06.058
No.

517
00:27:07.234 --> 00:27:08.539
I think it was intentional.

518
00:27:08.627 --> 00:27:10.716
But why?

519
00:27:17.461 --> 00:27:19.376
All auxiliary power
to the shields.

520
00:27:19.507 --> 00:27:22.771
Give me as much time as possible
inside that radiation zone.

521
00:27:22.902 --> 00:27:24.381
We're going after 'em.

522
00:27:30.257 --> 00:27:32.651
MITCHELL: We've got
another CME flare coming.

523
00:27:36.132 --> 00:27:37.786
-[grunting]
-[alarms sounding]

524
00:27:39.309 --> 00:27:41.877
-She's coding.
-The Gorn hatchlings are activating.

525
00:27:42.878 --> 00:27:44.488
Something has
accelerated their growth.

526
00:27:44.619 --> 00:27:46.795
A 14% chance of survival is
better than certain death.

527
00:27:49.711 --> 00:27:52.366
Let's prep her for surgery.

528
00:27:59.155 --> 00:28:01.288
UHURA: I'm still getting a
ping on the wolkite signal.

529
00:28:01.375 --> 00:28:03.943
UNA: We need to get to our
people while we still can.

530
00:28:04.073 --> 00:28:07.163
The magnetic fields here
make navigation impossible.

531
00:28:07.250 --> 00:28:09.600
UNA: That explains why the
Gorn go into a free fall.

532
00:28:09.731 --> 00:28:12.560
They let the intense gravity
wells do most of the work.

533
00:28:12.691 --> 00:28:14.475
No response from Starfleet.

534
00:28:14.605 --> 00:28:16.172
UNA: It's all the radiation.

535
00:28:16.303 --> 00:28:17.700
MITCHELL: And no
visuals on the ship

536
00:28:17.783 --> 00:28:20.002
or what's beyond
the binary stars.

537
00:28:20.133 --> 00:28:22.918
UNA: The light bends in a way
that creates a natural hologram.

538
00:28:23.049 --> 00:28:25.229
They're essentially invisible
once they pass through it.

539
00:28:25.312 --> 00:28:27.009
Makes for a great
defense system.

540
00:28:27.183 --> 00:28:29.011
MITCHELL: Maybe it's
a landing sequence.

541
00:28:29.142 --> 00:28:30.839
Could this be the
Gorn homeworld?

542
00:28:31.710 --> 00:28:34.234
If it is. that's how
they go back to it.

543
00:28:36.236 --> 00:28:37.585
[alarm chirps]

544
00:28:37.716 --> 00:28:38.978
MITCHELL: Captain.

545
00:28:39.152 --> 00:28:40.936
-something's moving out there.
-On screen.

546
00:28:54.123 --> 00:28:55.255
Number One.

547
00:29:04.177 --> 00:29:05.918
UNA: I've plotted
their trajectory.

548
00:29:06.092 --> 00:29:07.880
Those ships are headed straight
for Federation territory.

549
00:29:07.963 --> 00:29:10.313
-Warn Starfleet.
-It's a deep space relay.

550
00:29:10.444 --> 00:29:12.189
I won't be able to confirm
if they receive it.

551
00:29:12.272 --> 00:29:13.447
We need to go.

552
00:29:13.577 --> 00:29:15.275
Get clear of this
system's interference.

553
00:29:15.362 --> 00:29:16.628
Captain. if we lose our
lock on the wolkite signal.

554
00:29:16.711 --> 00:29:18.757
I'm not sure we can
reestablish contact.

555
00:29:18.887 --> 00:29:21.585
We'll lose the landing
party and the colonists.

556
00:29:23.457 --> 00:29:26.460
We can drop a long-range
communication buoy.

557
00:29:26.590 --> 00:29:27.853
Tie a signal to it.

558
00:29:27.983 --> 00:29:30.507
That way we can
come back for them.

559
00:29:30.638 --> 00:29:32.379
It's the best I've got.

560
00:29:32.553 --> 00:29:33.815
Do it.

561
00:29:35.251 --> 00:29:36.992
We have to stop this invasion.

562
00:29:37.079 --> 00:29:38.820
Communication buoy is deployed.

563
00:29:38.951 --> 00:29:40.604
Mitchell. stay on
that enemy fleet.

564
00:29:40.735 --> 00:29:42.432
-Bringing her about.
-As soon as we can.

565
00:29:42.563 --> 00:29:43.912
you warp out of here.

566
00:29:44.086 --> 00:29:45.784
Full throttle until we
can alert Starfleet.

567
00:29:47.307 --> 00:29:49.918
We're the only hope the
Federation's got right now.

568
00:29:56.751 --> 00:29:59.449
Computer. engage
quarantine mode.

569
00:30:00.494 --> 00:30:03.671
<i>COMPUTER: Quarantine
mode engaged.</i>

570
00:30:16.989 --> 00:30:20.166
If this goes sideways. it's.
it's Valeo Beta all over again.

571
00:30:20.296 --> 00:30:22.646
The probability of a
full-scale Gorn outbreak...

572
00:30:22.733 --> 00:30:24.692
I really don't want to know.

573
00:30:30.089 --> 00:30:33.657
Nurse Chapel. USS <i>Enterprise...</i>

574
00:30:35.224 --> 00:30:37.226
...injecting Patient Batel

575
00:30:37.357 --> 00:30:40.099
with experimental
plasma solution.

576
00:30:46.192 --> 00:30:48.368
-Anything. Ensign?
-UHURA: Still jammed. sir.

577
00:30:48.542 --> 00:30:51.458
The Gorn are transmitting
an interference signal.

578
00:30:52.459 --> 00:30:55.070
How long before we clear these
binary stars and go to warp?

579
00:30:55.201 --> 00:30:56.724
Not soon enough.

580
00:30:56.811 --> 00:30:58.512
Those Gorn ships are moving
a lot faster than we are.

581
00:30:58.595 --> 00:31:00.732
By the time we get a signal out.
the Gorn will be right on top

582
00:31:00.815 --> 00:31:01.907
of the outer Federation worlds.

583
00:31:01.990 --> 00:31:03.949
They're sitting ducks.

584
00:31:04.079 --> 00:31:06.125
Mitchell. are we in shooting
distance of the Gorn?

585
00:31:06.255 --> 00:31:07.517
[scoffs]: Chris.

586
00:31:07.648 --> 00:31:10.042
<i>Enterprise</i> against
an entire armada?

587
00:31:11.565 --> 00:31:13.349
We wouldn't stand a chance.

588
00:31:15.699 --> 00:31:17.353
[sighs]

589
00:31:23.794 --> 00:31:26.710
-Pike to science lab.
-[comms chime]

590
00:31:26.797 --> 00:31:28.538
Pelia. I need you on the bridge.

591
00:31:28.669 --> 00:31:30.627
<i>PELIA [over comms]: Aye.
Captain. right away.</i>

592
00:31:30.714 --> 00:31:32.151
What are you up to?

593
00:31:33.500 --> 00:31:35.676
You and Uhura.

594
00:31:35.806 --> 00:31:37.634
you said stellar
flares can dictate

595
00:31:37.765 --> 00:31:40.289
a Gorn's hunting
and resting cycles.

596
00:31:40.463 --> 00:31:42.335
UHURA: Right.

597
00:31:42.465 --> 00:31:43.862
We even know precisely what
kind of radiation signature

598
00:31:43.945 --> 00:31:45.599
would tell the Gorn
to go to sleep.

599
00:31:45.773 --> 00:31:49.124
-Um. sir. that's just a theory.
-[door whooshes open]

600
00:31:50.082 --> 00:31:51.213
PIKE: So...

601
00:31:52.649 --> 00:31:54.289
...we just need to
create a stellar flare.

602
00:31:54.390 --> 00:31:55.950
SCOTTY: Oh. forgive
me for interrupting.

603
00:31:56.044 --> 00:31:57.884
but you cannot make a
star do much of anything.

604
00:31:58.003 --> 00:32:00.048
Certainly not
precisely. Captain.

605
00:32:00.179 --> 00:32:01.963
Which is why we need
to become a CME. uh.

606
00:32:02.094 --> 00:32:03.399
X-flare ourselves.

607
00:32:03.530 --> 00:32:05.140
[chuckles] Eh...

608
00:32:05.271 --> 00:32:07.360
Captain. look. Uh.
sorry. do you mind?

609
00:32:07.447 --> 00:32:09.231
Eh. sure. using the ship

610
00:32:09.362 --> 00:32:10.584
would allow us to modulate
the exact radiation

611
00:32:10.667 --> 00:32:12.713
and EM signals we'd emit.

612
00:32:12.843 --> 00:32:14.323
But you're basically
talking about

613
00:32:14.410 --> 00:32:16.282
turning the ship into
an artificial star.

614
00:32:16.412 --> 00:32:17.848
That's-that's nearly impossible.

615
00:32:17.979 --> 00:32:19.938
-But not impossible.
-[stammers]

616
00:32:20.068 --> 00:32:21.809
To do that. we'd
have to go deeper

617
00:32:21.940 --> 00:32:23.593
into this deadly radiation zone.

618
00:32:23.680 --> 00:32:26.683
fly right between those binary
stars out there. and create

619
00:32:26.857 --> 00:32:29.121
some kind of competing
magnetic field

620
00:32:29.251 --> 00:32:31.471
to draw particles away
from both of them.

621
00:32:31.601 --> 00:32:34.822
Modify the deflector shields.
comms array. and. well...

622
00:32:34.909 --> 00:32:36.867
[sighs] every-everything
else. really.

623
00:32:36.998 --> 00:32:39.653
SCOTTY: Magnetize the hull
to attract stellar material.

624
00:32:39.827 --> 00:32:41.655
It's one in a thousand
we'd get it done right

625
00:32:41.829 --> 00:32:44.919
or don't blow ourselves up
along the way. and. look.

626
00:32:48.314 --> 00:32:50.055
Yeah. I don't know.
I like those odds.

627
00:32:50.229 --> 00:32:52.013
We'll just...

628
00:32:53.145 --> 00:32:55.103
...turn it off
before we blow up.

629
00:32:59.064 --> 00:33:01.196
Get it done.

630
00:33:01.327 --> 00:33:05.287
CHAPEL: Patient is responding
favorably to the transfusion.

631
00:33:05.418 --> 00:33:07.463
Ready to make the
first incision.

632
00:33:23.740 --> 00:33:26.265
♪ ♪

633
00:33:41.367 --> 00:33:43.412
Wait.

634
00:33:46.763 --> 00:33:49.984
You know the most likely outcome
is the death of Captain Batel?

635
00:33:50.071 --> 00:33:52.639
We just have to
have a little faith.

636
00:33:52.769 --> 00:33:55.555
Perhaps we are looking at this
from the wrong perspective.

637
00:33:56.643 --> 00:33:58.297
Instead of operating on Batel.

638
00:33:58.471 --> 00:34:00.255
what if we treated the
Gorn inside of her?

639
00:34:01.474 --> 00:34:03.650
We know they emerge to
feed. What if we feed them?

640
00:34:04.651 --> 00:34:08.350
Satiate them to keep
them from coming out.

641
00:34:09.525 --> 00:34:11.314
And when they are no
longer in defensive mode.

642
00:34:11.397 --> 00:34:13.573
-dissolve them.
-And use Una's Illyrian plasma

643
00:34:13.660 --> 00:34:15.492
to fight the multitude of
infections that will result

644
00:34:15.575 --> 00:34:18.056
-from their reabsorption.
-Yes.

645
00:34:19.361 --> 00:34:22.408
But we don't have enough time
to run another simulation.

646
00:34:22.538 --> 00:34:26.064
As you suggested. perhaps
we just need a little faith.

647
00:34:45.300 --> 00:34:47.476
ORTEGAS: Did we lose them?

648
00:34:47.563 --> 00:34:50.044
M'BENGA: Maybe. but if so.

649
00:34:50.131 --> 00:34:51.698
then not for long.

650
00:34:53.134 --> 00:34:55.528
LA'AN: This is an interface.

651
00:34:55.658 --> 00:34:58.313
They had them on the Gorn...
the Gorn breeding planet.

652
00:35:01.011 --> 00:35:02.970
My brother Manu. he...

653
00:35:05.320 --> 00:35:06.843
<i>MANU: Don't be afraid.</i>

654
00:35:06.974 --> 00:35:08.541
<i>Keep moving. no matter what.</i>

655
00:35:08.671 --> 00:35:10.195
M'BENGA: Hey.

656
00:35:13.850 --> 00:35:15.809
Hey.

657
00:35:17.202 --> 00:35:18.594
Are you okay?

658
00:35:20.683 --> 00:35:23.947
You're here now. not back there.

659
00:35:24.992 --> 00:35:27.386
Yeah. but here's not
great either. is it?

660
00:35:28.387 --> 00:35:30.389
No. I suppose not.

661
00:35:36.003 --> 00:35:38.571
LA'AN: I remember.
Let me try something.

662
00:36:01.071 --> 00:36:02.551
This is amazing.

663
00:36:02.682 --> 00:36:06.207
I'd love to take this apart.
figure out how it works.

664
00:36:06.294 --> 00:36:07.560
Yeah. good idea. Let's
make a whole day of it.

665
00:36:07.643 --> 00:36:09.341
Get snacks. hang out.

666
00:36:10.690 --> 00:36:12.648
M'BENGA: Those look
like buffer signatures.

667
00:36:12.779 --> 00:36:16.043
They are. And the
transport codes.

668
00:36:17.131 --> 00:36:19.046
If we can get this
to the <i>Enterprise.</i>

669
00:36:19.177 --> 00:36:21.266
then we can save the colonists.

670
00:36:22.484 --> 00:36:23.703
All of them.

671
00:36:24.747 --> 00:36:27.272
-[screeching]
-Guys...

672
00:36:43.201 --> 00:36:46.204
♪

673
00:36:55.256 --> 00:36:56.910
Get to the ship!

674
00:37:08.922 --> 00:37:10.315
[screeches. growls]

675
00:37:11.838 --> 00:37:13.274
[screeching]

676
00:37:14.144 --> 00:37:15.624
[yelling]

677
00:37:15.755 --> 00:37:17.583
[grunts]

678
00:37:17.713 --> 00:37:19.106
[yelling]

679
00:37:19.193 --> 00:37:21.021
[grunts. gasps]

680
00:37:23.110 --> 00:37:24.851
-[growls]
-[Ortegas wheezes]

681
00:37:29.247 --> 00:37:31.423
-[weapon whirring]
-[grunts]

682
00:37:36.950 --> 00:37:38.081
<i>MITCHELL: We are in position.</i>

683
00:37:38.168 --> 00:37:40.475
approaching the binary stars.

684
00:37:40.606 --> 00:37:43.391
UNA: The moment we shut
down the EM emitter.

685
00:37:43.478 --> 00:37:46.220
every single Gorn ship
is going to come at us.

686
00:37:46.351 --> 00:37:47.830
Like moths to a flame.

687
00:37:47.961 --> 00:37:49.354
Which is exactly what we want.

688
00:37:51.878 --> 00:37:53.183
Everybody ready?

689
00:38:00.539 --> 00:38:02.105
Make us shine like the sun.

690
00:38:12.551 --> 00:38:14.857
♪ ♪

691
00:38:26.347 --> 00:38:28.741
-[panting]
-[Gorn screeching]

692
00:38:28.871 --> 00:38:30.482
[Ortegas grunts]

693
00:38:31.874 --> 00:38:33.572
-[loud bang]
-ORTEGAS: The pilot seat.

694
00:38:33.702 --> 00:38:35.138
Put me in the pilot seat.

695
00:38:35.269 --> 00:38:36.269
Put me in the pilot seat!

696
00:38:36.401 --> 00:38:37.576
Forget about it!

697
00:38:37.663 --> 00:38:39.752
I can fly it. It has to be me.

698
00:38:39.882 --> 00:38:41.057
She's right. We need to go.

699
00:38:42.798 --> 00:38:44.887
[pained groans]

700
00:38:49.022 --> 00:38:50.458
[groans with effort]

701
00:38:52.808 --> 00:38:54.027
[sighs]

702
00:38:57.422 --> 00:38:59.075
[chuckles weakly]

703
00:39:04.211 --> 00:39:06.126
[grunting softly]

704
00:39:15.788 --> 00:39:17.311
[grunting]

705
00:39:24.144 --> 00:39:25.363
[Ortegas grunting]

706
00:39:27.539 --> 00:39:28.844
Ah!

707
00:39:28.975 --> 00:39:30.846
[screeches]

708
00:39:32.892 --> 00:39:34.067
[grunts]

709
00:39:35.460 --> 00:39:37.462
[gasping]

710
00:39:45.470 --> 00:39:47.167
[snarls]

711
00:39:49.169 --> 00:39:50.823
[alarm blaring]

712
00:39:53.782 --> 00:39:56.742
We're covered in beta
particles and gamma rays.

713
00:39:56.872 --> 00:39:58.961
This ship is hitting
critical levels of radiation!

714
00:39:59.092 --> 00:40:00.619
-What are the Gorn doing?
-MITCHELL: They have broken ranks.

715
00:40:00.702 --> 00:40:03.052
currently on intercept
course with <i>Enterprise.</i>

716
00:40:03.183 --> 00:40:04.445
All right. so far. so good.

717
00:40:04.576 --> 00:40:05.896
Now let's see if
they shoot at us.

718
00:40:08.754 --> 00:40:11.104
Captain. I have a
signal bouncing off

719
00:40:11.191 --> 00:40:12.497
the communications beacon.

720
00:40:13.628 --> 00:40:14.628
It's La'An. sir.

721
00:40:16.457 --> 00:40:18.594
<i>-Enterprise.</i> are you there?
<i>-PIKE: La'An. where are you?</i>

722
00:40:18.677 --> 00:40:20.592
On our way. If
you can read me.

723
00:40:20.722 --> 00:40:22.202
I'm sending you transport codes.

724
00:40:22.376 --> 00:40:23.936
<i>[breaking up]: Beam
the Parnassians out.</i>

725
00:40:24.770 --> 00:40:25.949
<i>PIKE: We're trying
to beam you out.</i>

726
00:40:26.032 --> 00:40:27.037
but we're having
trouble getting a lock.

727
00:40:27.120 --> 00:40:28.338
Do you copy?

728
00:40:29.992 --> 00:40:31.037
They're gaining on us!

729
00:40:31.211 --> 00:40:32.081
<i>Enterprise.</i> do you read me?

730
00:40:32.168 --> 00:40:33.300
Beam the Parnassians out.

731
00:40:33.431 --> 00:40:35.737
-[explosion]
-[pained grunt]

732
00:40:47.140 --> 00:40:48.446
[screeches]

733
00:40:55.583 --> 00:40:58.151
Captain. hull integrity is
approaching critical failure!

734
00:40:58.325 --> 00:41:00.153
♪

735
00:41:10.903 --> 00:41:13.166
Turn it off. Turn it off!

736
00:41:13.296 --> 00:41:15.734
[alarm blaring]

737
00:41:21.783 --> 00:41:24.351
Did it work?

738
00:41:24.482 --> 00:41:26.396
Aye. sir. the last of
the Gorn have gone home.

739
00:41:27.267 --> 00:41:29.791
What about the Parnassians?
Did we get them out in time?

740
00:41:29.922 --> 00:41:31.663
UHURA: Yes. Captain.

741
00:41:31.750 --> 00:41:33.230
The transport codes
from La'An worked.

742
00:41:33.316 --> 00:41:35.188
Several hundred
colonists accounted for

743
00:41:35.318 --> 00:41:37.190
and headed for the
overflow infirmary.

744
00:41:38.191 --> 00:41:40.240
<i>LA'AN [breaking up]: Captain.
we need immediate as...</i>

745
00:41:40.323 --> 00:41:42.587
Beam us out and have a
medical team standing by.

746
00:41:44.066 --> 00:41:46.416
Pike to Engineering?

747
00:41:46.591 --> 00:41:48.161
<i>SCOTTY [over comms]: Aye. Captain.
we're using the transport codes</i>

748
00:41:48.244 --> 00:41:51.160
<i>to hack into the Gorn hunter.
should be just a moment.</i>

749
00:41:52.640 --> 00:41:55.643
UNA: Chris. Chris. we did it.

750
00:41:55.730 --> 00:41:57.471
We triggered a long
hibernation in the Gorn.

751
00:41:57.602 --> 00:41:58.994
PIKE: Yeah...

752
00:41:59.995 --> 00:42:01.566
But I can't help wondering
if we didn't just create

753
00:42:01.649 --> 00:42:03.433
a problem for someone
else to solve later.

754
00:42:03.608 --> 00:42:05.305
[comms beeping]

755
00:42:05.435 --> 00:42:08.482
Captain. I'm getting a secure
channel from Admiral April.

756
00:42:08.656 --> 00:42:09.831
Put him through.

757
00:42:11.964 --> 00:42:14.357
<i>APRIL: Chris. We just got
your priority message.</i>

758
00:42:14.488 --> 00:42:16.189
<i>How much time do we have
before the Gorn ships get here?</i>

759
00:42:16.272 --> 00:42:17.839
Ignore last transmission.

760
00:42:17.926 --> 00:42:19.932
We won't be seeing the Gorn.
at least not for a while.

761
00:42:20.015 --> 00:42:21.756
<i>APRIL: How certain are you?</i>

762
00:42:21.930 --> 00:42:24.672
Let's just say I found
a way to punch back.

763
00:42:25.455 --> 00:42:27.327
[panting]

764
00:42:29.372 --> 00:42:31.766
♪ ♪

765
00:42:35.596 --> 00:42:39.252
Stay with me. Stay with me.

766
00:42:39.339 --> 00:42:41.341
[labored breathing]

767
00:42:42.298 --> 00:42:44.562
[weakly]: I did good.

768
00:42:44.692 --> 00:42:45.737
Didn't I?

769
00:42:45.911 --> 00:42:49.654
Stop. You're going to make it.

770
00:42:52.744 --> 00:42:54.354
They'll have to try
harder than that.

771
00:42:55.877 --> 00:42:59.141
I'm Erica Ortegas.

772
00:42:59.272 --> 00:43:00.969
I fly the ship.

773
00:43:01.100 --> 00:43:04.103
M'BENGA: Hold on. I got you.

774
00:43:11.893 --> 00:43:13.852
[electricity crackles]

775
00:43:15.593 --> 00:43:17.769
[door whooshes shut]

776
00:43:17.943 --> 00:43:19.640
We did all we could.

777
00:43:20.641 --> 00:43:22.643
It's in Captain
Batel's hands now.

778
00:43:23.470 --> 00:43:24.732
Indeed.

779
00:43:31.521 --> 00:43:32.827
Thank you.

780
00:43:33.828 --> 00:43:36.091
I couldn't have done
that without you.

781
00:43:36.178 --> 00:43:37.745
You're welcome.

782
00:43:52.978 --> 00:43:54.675
How is she?

783
00:43:54.806 --> 00:43:56.590
She's in the lab.
still in recovery.

784
00:43:56.764 --> 00:43:58.418
[door whooshes open]

785
00:44:00.420 --> 00:44:01.682
[door whooshes shut]

786
00:44:08.297 --> 00:44:10.125
[door whooshes open]

787
00:44:10.256 --> 00:44:12.084
<i>UNA [over comms]: Landing
Party accounted for</i>

788
00:44:12.258 --> 00:44:13.524
<i>and getting treatment in
the overflow infirmary.</i>

789
00:44:13.607 --> 00:44:15.130
<i>Erica is critical...</i>

790
00:44:15.304 --> 00:44:16.958
<i>but stable.</i>

791
00:44:17.089 --> 00:44:19.004
Thanks for the update.

792
00:44:19.134 --> 00:44:20.875
Once we clear the
radiation bands.

793
00:44:21.006 --> 00:44:22.790
chart a course for
Earth. Warp us home.

794
00:44:22.877 --> 00:44:25.445
<i>UNA: Of course.
Number One out.</i>

795
00:44:40.373 --> 00:44:41.766
[door whooshes shut]

796
00:44:55.562 --> 00:44:56.781
Okay.

797
00:44:57.825 --> 00:44:59.131
Okay. Dad.

798
00:45:00.523 --> 00:45:02.264
You win.

799
00:45:04.614 --> 00:45:06.268
[sighs]

800
00:45:09.271 --> 00:45:11.883
Our Father.

801
00:45:12.057 --> 00:45:13.188
who art in heaven...

802
00:45:13.362 --> 00:45:14.668
Chris?

803
00:45:16.322 --> 00:45:17.932
You're awake.

804
00:45:18.063 --> 00:45:21.022
Yeah. Which I assume means

805
00:45:21.109 --> 00:45:24.243
that tiny Gorn didn't
pop out of my body

806
00:45:24.373 --> 00:45:26.071
and kill everybody.

807
00:45:26.245 --> 00:45:27.463
No.

808
00:45:27.594 --> 00:45:30.989
No. no. no. We're still here.

809
00:45:31.163 --> 00:45:33.774
Spock and Chapel came up
with a treatment. uh...

810
00:45:33.948 --> 00:45:35.950
I'll have them walk you
through it later. but...

811
00:45:37.386 --> 00:45:39.301
...you're still not
out of the woods yet.

812
00:45:40.476 --> 00:45:41.739
How?

813
00:45:43.523 --> 00:45:44.785
Una helped.

814
00:45:47.005 --> 00:45:48.615
Chris. you shouldn't
have done that.

815
00:45:48.746 --> 00:45:51.749
Marie. I've already lost
too much. all right?

816
00:45:51.879 --> 00:45:54.012
So we can sit here
and we can argue about

817
00:45:54.186 --> 00:45:55.970
what might or might not
happen in the future.

818
00:45:56.144 --> 00:45:59.104
or you can just set all that
aside and let me hold you.

819
00:45:59.234 --> 00:46:00.801
[sighs]

820
00:46:03.630 --> 00:46:05.893
I really don't want to lose you.

821
00:46:13.509 --> 00:46:15.511
I'm still here.

822
00:46:18.340 --> 00:46:20.125
I'm still here.

